{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "kjv-job-029",
  "collection": "kjv-bible",
  "document_type": "bible_chapter",
  "number": 29,
  "title": "Job 29",
  "display_title": "Job 29",
  "translation": "King James Version",
  "translationCode": "KJV",
  "bookId": "job",
  "book": "Job",
  "bookName": "Job",
  "bookOrder": 18,
  "testament": "old",
  "chapter": 29,
  "sortOrder": 18029,
  "verseCount": 25,
  "aliases": [
    "Job"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:29:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "Moreover Job continued his parable, and said,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 29:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:29:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:29:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "Oh that I were as in months past, as in the days when God preserved me;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 29:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:29:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:29:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "When his candle shined upon my head, and when by his light I walked through darkness;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 29:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:29:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:29:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "As I was in the days of my youth, when the secret of God was upon my tabernacle;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 29:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:29:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:29:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "When the Almighty was yet with me, when my children were about me;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 29:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:29:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:29:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "When I washed my steps with butter, and the rock poured me out rivers of oil;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 29:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:29:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:29:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "When I went out to the gate through the city, when I prepared my seat in the street!",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 29:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:29:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:29:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "The young men saw me, and hid themselves: and the aged arose, and stood up.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 29:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:29:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:29:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "The princes refrained talking, and laid their hand on their mouth.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 29:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:29:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:29:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "The nobles held their peace, and their tongue cleaved to the roof of their mouth.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 29:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:29:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:29:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "When the ear heard me, then it blessed me; and when the eye saw me, it gave witness to me:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 29:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:29:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:29:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "Because I delivered the poor that cried, and the fatherless, and him that had none to help him.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 29:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:29:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:29:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "The blessing of him that was ready to perish came upon me: and I caused the widow’s heart to sing for joy.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 29:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:29:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:29:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "I put on righteousness, and it clothed me: my judgment was as a robe and a diadem.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 29:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:29:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:29:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "I was eyes to the blind, and feet was I to the lame.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 29:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:29:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:29:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "I was a father to the poor: and the cause which I knew not I searched out.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 29:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:29:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:29:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "And I brake the jaws of the wicked, and plucked the spoil out of his teeth.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 29:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:29:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:29:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "Then I said, I shall die in my nest, and I shall multiply my days as the sand.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 29:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:29:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-019",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 19,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:29:19",
      "numberLabel": "19",
      "text": "My root was spread out by the waters, and the dew lay all night upon my branch.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 29:19",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:29:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-020",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 20,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:29:20",
      "numberLabel": "20",
      "text": "My glory was fresh in me, and my bow was renewed in my hand.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 29:20",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:29:20"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-021",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 21,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:29:21",
      "numberLabel": "21",
      "text": "Unto me men gave ear, and waited, and kept silence at my counsel.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 29:21",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:29:21"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-022",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 22,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:29:22",
      "numberLabel": "22",
      "text": "After my words they spake not again; and my speech dropped upon them.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 29:22",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:29:22"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-023",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 23,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:29:23",
      "numberLabel": "23",
      "text": "And they waited for me as for the rain; and they opened their mouth wide as for the latter rain.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 29:23",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:29:23"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-024",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 24,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:29:24",
      "numberLabel": "24",
      "text": "If I laughed on them, they believed it not; and the light of my countenance they cast not down.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 29:24",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:29:24"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-025",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 25,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:29:25",
      "numberLabel": "25",
      "text": "I chose out their way, and sat chief, and dwelt as a king in the army, as one that comforteth the mourners.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 29:25",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:29:25"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
